================================================================================
Note on the capture library
================================================================================

This repository contains no GPL code. It links against libwebaudio, which the
user installs separately:

    https://github.com/lovemilk2333/linux-web-audio-capture   (GPL-3.0-or-later)

That library is a derivative work of Sunshine and so must be GPL-3.0. The
consequence, which matters the moment you redistribute anything built from this
repository: a binary linked against libwebaudio is a combined work, and the GPL
covers that combined work however the linking is done. Dynamic linking is not a
boundary under the GPL; that mechanism belongs to the LGPL.

So this source is BSD-3-Clause, while a binary built from it and linked against
libwebaudio is GPL-3.0 when you convey it, and has to come with the
corresponding source under GPL-3.0 terms. Running such a binary yourself, or
building it for your own use, carries no such obligation.

See the Licence section of README.md.
